# ModemManager: do not let the idle IP_SW0 netdev compete with IP_HW0 for bearers
#
# This board exposes TWO net ports from mhi_net:
#   mhi_swip0  <- MHI channel 46/47  (IP_SW0),  ifindex 5
#   mhi_hwip0  <- MHI channel 100/101 (IP_HW0), ifindex 6
#
# ModemManager picks a data port with mm_base_modem_peek_best_data_port(),
# which returns the FIRST not-connected port of the requested type.  That is
# enumeration order, not "the channel the modem actually uses": IP_SW0 is
# registered before IP_HW0, so a bearer could be created on mhi_swip0 and then
# silently carry nothing.
#
# Everything we have measured says the data path is IP_HW0: the WDA data format
# is queried/applied on endpoint pcie/4, kebab-qmi-wds.py binds and starts the
# call on mhi_hwip0, and kebab-modem-tx-probe proves packets reach the IP_HW0
# UL ring.  So mark the SW port as ignored for MM and make the choice
# deterministic.
#
# Applied after 77-mm-sdx55-fusion.rules (udev runs these files in lexical
# order), so the ignore flag wins over the candidate tagging there.
SUBSYSTEM=="net", KERNEL=="mhi_swip*", ENV{ID_MM_PORT_IGNORE}="1"
